From 1dc4fa6973dd0203823bd554cf6617f1dac669af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ron D." <8740514+rgnv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:51:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/29] wasm-port: render the 1.32 world end-to-end (client map
 registration, unit model resolver, fog completeness)

Three root causes fixed for the Reforged 1.32 data on both native and
emscripten builds:

- CL_BeginLoadingMap now registers the map with the renderer
  (re.RegisterMap was previously only ever called with NULL, so terrain
  layers were never built: layers=0 -> world pass empty).
- g_metadata: the 1.32 UnitUI.slk dropped the model 'file' column; units
  and buildings now resolve their models from the retail tree layout
  (units/<race>/<name>/<name>.mdx, buildings/...) via a resolver with a
  raw-id fallback. Previously every spawn fell to NOCLIENT (no models,
  no sight, no fog reveal).
- r_fogofwar: the client fog network texture now gets explicit
  GL_NEAREST/LINEAR + CLAMP_TO_EDGE parameters after upload. Desktop GL
  sampled the base level of an incomplete texture anyway; strict WebGL2
  returns black, which made the wasm world render fogged-black.

Also: BlzCreateUnitWithSkin API, W3DBG instrumentation probes (to be
stripped before release), misc API surface additions from the bootybay +
Blizzard.j native diff.
